#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cleave — partition a function into the argument worlds its callers inhabit.

A function is not one function. It is the set of specializations its call
sites actually exercise. Coverage says a line ran. grep lists every call.
Neither answers: do tests and production live in the same worlds?

Exit codes:
  0  ok (or --check with no tilts)
  1  --check found one or more tilts
  2  usage / tool error
"""
